      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I'll create the improved test file in my working directory.The improved test compiled successfully. The changes made for better understandability:\n\n1. **Removed unused imports** — dropped `assertEquals`, `assertFalse`, `assertSame`, `assertTrue`, serialization classes, `Duration`, `LocalTime`, and `EqualsTester` which were never used in this test.\n2. **Removed the unused `data_valid()` method** — it existed in the original class but was never referenced by any test method, making it dead code that confused readers.\n3. **Formatted `data_invalid()` one entry per line** — the original crammed all 13 strings onto a single line; each entry now has its own line.\n4. **Added grouping comments** — short inline comments explain *why* each group of strings is invalid (missing `P` prefix, wrong unit order, unsupported week designator, etc.), making the intent of each test case immediately clear."
